 powerful, and we recommend you take some time to read their documentation if you
 are building complex prompts.
 
+### Environment-conditional filters
+
+The `conditional_filters` argument on `@outlines.prompt`, `Prompt.from_str`, and
+`Prompt.from_file` selects one mapping of custom Jinja filters when a prompt is
+constructed. Standard conditions are checked in this order:
+
+1. `debug` when `OUTLINES_DEBUG=true`;
+2. `production` when `ENVIRONMENT=production`;
+3. `testing` when `ENV=testing`, `OUTLINES_TESTING=true`, or
+   `TESTING_MODE=on`.
+
+Names and values use ASCII case-insensitive exact comparisons. An active
+standard condition missing from the mapping is skipped; if none matches, the
+alphabetically first supplied key is selected. `None` and an empty mapping add
+no filters.
+
+Selection is captured by the new prompt and later environment changes do not
+alter it. Only filters from the selected condition are installed, including for
+file includes and inheritance. They may replace Jinja and Outlines filters for
+that prompt.
+
 
